#[section, $md:
    Boracle is a developer-facing reference model of borrow legality, not a language feature and not a production fallback. It exists so borrow reasoning can be inspected, compared and extended outside the production checker.

    This page carries two documents: the reference solver, and the operational contract for the bounded oracle that executes normalized problems.

    @https://github.com/nyejames/moth/blob/main/docs/roadmap/plans/production-borrow-checker.md (Production borrow checker and Boracle development) tracks the live alpha implementation, performance findings and actionable research-to-production follow-ups.

    @../checked-proof-budget-research (Checked proof-budget research) records how current experiments should preserve room for a future opt-in deep analysis tier without turning Boracle into a public fallback checker.
]

#[section, reference_content]

#[section, operational_content]
